# App Router

## Route groups

- `(dashboard)` — authenticated shell (`RequireAuth` → `SetupGuard` → `DashboardLayout`)
- `(setup)` — onboarding wizard (auth required, minimal chrome)
- Public auth: `/login`, `/signup`, `/forgot-password` (no route group)

## Thin page pattern

`page.tsx` should be a server wrapper that delegates to a feature component:

```tsx
import { Suspense } from "react";
import { LoadingState } from "@/components/shared/loading-state";
import { FeaturePage } from "@/components/<feature>/<feature>-page";

export default function Page() {
  return (
    <Suspense fallback={<LoadingState />}>
      <FeaturePage />
    </Suspense>
  );
}
```

Use `Suspense` when children call `useSearchParams()`.

## Conventions

- Client logic lives in `src/components/`, not in `page.tsx`
- Dynamic detail routes: `[id]/page.tsx`
- New sidebar route: add `mainNavItems` entry **and** matching `(dashboard)/<slug>/page.tsx`
- API routes: `src/app/api/<name>/route.ts` with named exports (`GET`, `POST`, …)
- Global styles only in `src/app/globals.css`

## Next.js version

This project uses Next.js 16 with breaking changes. Read `node_modules/next/dist/docs/` before changing routing APIs.
